      "render": {
        "prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-cone}\n",
        "suffix": "\\end{definition}"
      },
      "risk_level": "R3",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "source_math_hash": "sha256:cfcce86d125534dbb050e475b55fd2f2f3334022d1a3794832bdeb8b9aa39257",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1057cdb717dec2642f329041d92985c16afa062b0644a34b03acccb3f2650aff",
      "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent\ngraded <MATH_0003>-algebra. Assume that <MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>Often one imposes the assumption that\n<MATH_0005> is generated by <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007>. We do not\nassume this in order to be consistent with <REF_0001>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>cone associated to <MATH_0008><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> or the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>affine cone associated to <MATH_0009><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nis\n<MATH_0010>\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:ea1ab50337bcc15c2d99b6fa6afdcc341959e332d8f3007b48f2428279038f78",
      "unit_id": "tag:062Q:statement"
    },
    {
      "chapter": "constructions",
      "node_kind": "paragraph",
      "parent_tag": "062P",
      "placeholders": {
        "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$",
        "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_{C(\\mathcal{A})} =\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0} \\mathcal{A}_n\n$$",
        "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"
      },
      "render": {
        "prefix": "",
        "suffix": ""
      },
      "risk_level": "R2",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "source_math_hash": "sha256:7fff8bafa5e8483f5daee6c6003a7ad1c1e718d76f769f70f3233ab502e09e6c",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ddc3414075cd1585ac6631b887c6dabbca0b636bfcc75d45f38b540d50baeb19",
      "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe cone associated to a graded sheaf of <MATH_0001>-algebras\ncomes with a bit of extra structure. Namely, we obtain a grading\n<MATH_0002>\nThus we can define an abstract cone as follows.\n\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:36f3b00965449979ab5d71700159459d36025f228b19286f3baab698952d8b3d",
      "unit_id": "tag:062P:prose-0002"
    },
    {
      "chapter": "constructions",
      "node_kind": "definition",
      "parent_tag": "062P",
      "placeholders": {
        "MATH_0001": "$S$",
        "MATH_0002": "$\\pi : C \\to S$",
        "MATH_0003": "$S$",
        "MATH_0004": "$\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_C$",
        "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$",
        "MATH_0006": "$\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_C = \\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0} \\mathcal{A}_n$",
        "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{A}_0 = \\mathcal{O}_S$",
        "MATH_0008": "$\\pi : C \\to S$",
        "MATH_0009": "$\\pi' : C' \\to S$",
        "MATH_0010": "$f : C \\to C'$",
        "MATH_0011": "$$\nf^* : \\pi'_*\\mathcal{O}_{C'} \\longrightarrow \\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_C\n$$",
        "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}",
        "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}",
        "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ",
        "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "
      },
      "render": {
        "prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-abstract-cone}\n",
        "suffix": "\\end{definition}"
      },
      "risk_level": "R3",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "source_math_hash": "sha256:434166c7fe419baee1062354776b972f703c110d87235d0521019104bdecc663",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a270776cb9c520cda5f1611d5fe852a9cbd1840a8b6dae4fe4cd64c6647a1dc",
      "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>cone <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is an\naffine morphism of schemes such that <MATH_0004> is endowed with\nthe structure of a graded <MATH_0005>-algebra\n<MATH_0006>\nsuch that <MATH_0007>. A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism of cones<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nfrom <MATH_0008> to <MATH_0009>\nis a morphism <MATH_0010> such that the induced map\n<MATH_0011>\nis compatible with the given gradings.\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:4a08f1d95ddf8f46ae6480af85b0588bc6251a2cf45cf3b376914f24c65da740",
      "unit_id": "tag:062R:statement"
    },
    {
      "chapter": "constructions",
      "node_kind": "paragraph",
      "parent_tag": "062P",
      "placeholders": {
        "MATH_0001": "$S$",
        "MATH_0002": "$S$",
        "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"
      },
      "render": {
        "prefix": "",
        "suffix": ""
      },
      "risk_level": "R2",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "source_math_hash": "sha256:3373d69d1a771d1b240d3f94798edce7e161caf54de4b2de49dd8524c8dc1502",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e5715a6340518a9a869ebbb72750b8cb10c9e7b418022d0c45cc42665307aace",
      "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAny vector bundle is an example of a cone. In fact the category of\nvector bundles over <MATH_0001> is a full subcategory of the category of cones\nover <MATH_0002>.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:25dc93202b46f2d38a334b0bdcb66845da37a2b71725bf53dafe46c8a04a0baf",
      "unit_id": "tag:062P:prose-0003"
    },
